# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env.local.
# Firebase values: Firebase console > project settings > your apps > novara-host (web).
#
# AUTH_DOMAIN must be the domain the app is actually served from, not the
# default <project>.firebaseapp.com. Browsers partition storage for a
# third-party auth handler, which breaks sign-in with "missing initial state"
# on iOS in-app browsers. Firebase Hosting serves /__/auth/* on every site,
# so pointing this at our own domain keeps the whole flow same-origin.
#
# Doing that has a consequence that is easy to miss and takes sign-in down
# completely. Moving AUTH_DOMAIN off <project>.firebaseapp.com moves the OAuth
# handler with it, and Google only accepts redirect URIs it has been told about.
# So for EVERY domain this app is served from, add both of these to the Google
# Cloud OAuth web client for novarasocial-dev ("Web client (auto created by
# Google Service)", APIs & Services > Credentials):
#
#     Authorized JavaScript origins   https://<domain>
#     Authorized redirect URIs        https://<domain>/__/auth/handler
#
# Skipping it fails as "Error 400: redirect_uri_mismatch". That is a Google
# error PAGE, not a Firebase SDK code, so it never reaches signInError and
# SignInPage renders nothing at all — the user just lands back on sign-in.
#
# Separately, and also required, every domain must be listed under Firebase
# console > Authentication > Settings > Authorized domains. That one fails as
# auth/unauthorized-domain, which DOES surface in the app.
#
# Both were missed on 2026-08-29 when host.novara.social was added, and host
# sign-in was broken until they were entered by hand. Google warns these take
# 5 minutes to a few hours to take effect.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# Amplitude browser API key. Analytics no-op locally when left blank.
VITE_AMPLITUDE_API_KEY=

# Google Calendar, F14. Web OAuth client id from its OWN Google Cloud project,
# deliberately not novarasocial-dev: calendar.readonly is a sensitive scope, and
# adding it to the Firebase project's consent screen would change what every
# Novara consumer user sees at sign in and could force a verification review.
# Setup steps: docs/Google_Calendar_Setup.md. Blank leaves the file import path
# working and hides the connect button.
VITE_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
